Other than asking NT questions in a Linux group, you mean? *g,d,r*

Is the CDROM you're using set for 512 byte sector size?
Never played with an AS200, but some Matsushita CDROMs have problems
booting VMS, as they don't understand the 10-byte SCSI enquiry, and go
into a reset state whilst the 6-byte fall-back enquiry is sent, so it
never arrives at the CDROM's firmware...
Then again, I have a Sony that my 3000/300L saw at every LUN, and the
Alpha had big issues with this.

I'm currently using a Matsu/Panasonic CR-503B in with my AXPpci33/noname
and that seems OK. Booted NT fine.

Just to make sure, check termination (at both ends, and a chicken/goat
over the centre) and check your drive is able to do 512-bytes/sector &
indeed jumpered as such.

Check the Sun-CDROM FAQ. That should tell you approximately if your drive
is suitable. Or maybe even the NT HCL.

Cheers
/dave


