In a previous article, "Yevgeniy G. Zolotukhin" <eugene@concentric.net> said:
>Somebody knows how to do X-Windoows on  Multia , aka UDB. Linux
>installs, but can not run X-windows, seems like TGA server is not yet
>developed completely.

Don't blame your own failures on your software.  There are hundreds of us
successfully running X windows on our UDBs.  I personally am doing 1280x1024
at 74Hz, and it rocks.  Too bad it's hardware limited to 8 bits for colour,
though.

Check the archives for the RedHat axp mailing list on their "Support" web
pages - some people have reported various problems with RedHat 5.1.  I'm using
RedHat 5.0 and it works just fine.  Some things to check:

1. That you are using the TGA driver, and not the VGA or some other one.
2. That you properly copied the memory address reported by /proc/pci into your
XF86Config file.
3. That you only have one Modeline defined.
4. That the Modeline you have defined works for your monitor.

Here are some of the relevant parts of my XF86Config:

Modeline "1280x1024"  135    1280 1312 1456 1712  1024 1027 1030 1064

ection "Device"
    Identifier  "TGA"
    VendorName  "DEC"
    BoardName   "ZLXp-E1"
    MemBase     0xa000000 
    #VideoRam    2048
    # Insert Clocks lines here if appropriate
EndSection
Section "Screen"
    Driver      "accel"
    Device      "TGA"
    #Device      "My Video Card"
    Monitor     "CTX 1785GMd"
    Subsection "Display"
        Depth       8
        Modes       "1280x1024"
        ViewPort    0 0
        Virtual     1280 1024
    EndSubsection
EndSection

-- 
