Hey man... I had a problem with my default TGA under Linux, too, at first.
What is the error you get when X kills off and won't start?  The one that I
got was that the display "needs membase". Basically what you have to do if
you get a membase error is to type the following on the command line:

"cat /proc/pci"

 look for your dispaly adapter in the list of PCI devices and copy down the
hex memory address for your TGA display.  You have to add that memory
address to the /usr/X11R6/lib/X11/XF86Config file.  You have to find the
graphics adapter section of that file and add a line that says "MemBase
0x000000" or whatever your memory address is.

If you are not getting a membase error and you feel like giving up on it,
try getting a graphics card that has the S3 chip in it...  Those work well.
Some ATI Mach 64's work, and Matrox cards usually work, but S3's cards most
often work in every alpha.

Later.
-John

