Azira (chenc@csus.edu) wrote:
: Personally with XFree86 and an Alpha that I know of only Matrox and S3 are
: supported.

S3 is a wide range of cards and some of them are S3Virge and the like.
"Personally" I was using on Alpha ATI-Mach64 cards, and various S3 and
various SVGA (Matrox including but as it happened no Trident).

: Matrox's are nice though.

I agree.  But I also have seen posting to the tune "You cannot make
Matrox to work on Alpha".  Hm....

The biggest issue is really not with Linux but with BIOS emulator
in firmware and also possibly in a loader.  It has to initialize a card
and for some it apparently fails.  When this will happen you will
be not able to load your kernel and that is about it.  You will see
"MACHINE CHECK" or a frozen machine.

Oh, one more thing about these few UX boards around.  The current
Linux loader software has problems with initializing video cards
behind PCI bridge; that means that you will have to stick your video
card into the only 64-bit PCI slot.  This is supposed to change RSN
but at the moment this is the situation.

  Michal



