I setup my AlphaStation200 4/166 (which I also got from Onsale) a few months
ago and I had almost the same set of problems. I took me forever to figure
out the right linload/milo/kernel combination to get this thing running. I
did get mine to work with the avanti-s.gz kernel.

The biggest (undocumented?) problem I found is that after the system loaded
milo the video picture was just a bunch of garbled lines flashing on the
screen. I though for sure the system was locked up but it wasn't. I finally
found a blurb in a support website that talked about viewing the console
output from another computer connected to the serial port (com1). It
worked - I could see the milo prompt and start the kernel using (boot
fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0  <or something similar to that>) After the
kernel loaded the output from com1 stopped and the video output from the
alpha was normal again. I used a win95 computer, a null modem cable, and
hyperterminal set to 9600/8/N/1 to view the alpha's console.

If I had known about the console output on com1 I could have configured and
installed RedHat in a couple of hours instead of 2 weeks. I also would have
known that I did pick the correct kernel (avanti-s) on my first attempt - I
just didn't know it because I thought the system was locking up.

My alpha came with a DEC TGA card which I later replaced with Diamond
Stealth 64.


