This is a thanks to those who offered help with my MILO problem on my
PC164 lx box.

Its working now, Linux (well X isn't) and Nt, but the short story is
that the documentation from both REDHAT and DCG (hardware vendor) was
simply unclear.

DCG specifies rawriting the milo image to a floppy.  This is incorrect
and of course destroys linload.exe.  They also don't mention  putting
linload.exe on a floppy. (this is page 26-27 of their users manual.)

REDHAT instructs you to enter the 'supplementary menu' in the
Alphabios menu.  There is none on this board.

The procedure is to:

1.  Make a dos floppy with linload .

2.  Make the ramdisk floppy and the bootdisk floppy using rawrite.

3.  In the Os selection menu, the bootfile is correct at
a:linload.exe.  However, since my pc164lx motherboard (samsung)
points the user  the cdrom, not the floppy drive.  So, point the OS
PATH to the CDROM and the location of MILO on the CD.  This should get
you to a MILO prompt.  (I confess to being a slave to the printed
documentation and not trying this much earlier in the process.)

4. The boot instructions from there are correct.  The result is the os
selection screen:  
Boot name: milo
 Boot file:Disk1, Partition 1 linload.exe
OS Path Disk1, Partition 1 \milo\lx164
OS Options:  boot hda2:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hda2

I hope this is of use to others, as this installation took way too
long.

thanks again to those who replied.

bill mccall




