What doesn't work, system date is wrong date after booting or clock keep
randomly skipping into the future?

If you have the wrong date after booting try this.

	Reboot computer so you have the wrong date.

	At the prompt type "clock -Ar"

		If date is correct then change ARC=true in /etc/sysconfig/clock

	else

	At the prompt type "clock -r"
	
		If date is correct then change ARC=false in /etc/sysconfig/clock

	Reboot

I have an ARC console, but strange enough I have to run clock without
having ARC=true.

