I'm trying to make my AXP work as a firewall, and I'm having a really
bad time.

I've upgraded (downgraded) the ipfwadm so it works, and I've got a
pretty common and standard rc.firewall -- my friend's also running the
same version of RedHat, and it works for him -- on an Intel box.

The problem is that my connection drops inexplicably when I connect
in.  I use ssh to enter my firewall.  I go from the outside world to
my firewall as root, then from my firewall to my internal machine as
me.  Every few minutes, I lose the ability to type -- well, that's not
quite true.  I lose the ability to see what I'm typing, and to see
updates or anything else in the screen.  It turns into a one-way
connection, all going inbound.

I have to kill the connection with ~. and restart the connection.  If
it weren't for "screen", I'd be insane by now.  Help!

Here's my current firewall rules:

/sbin/ipfwadm -F -p m
/sbin/ipfwadm -F -a m -S 10.74.84.0/24 -D 0.0.0.0/0

I'm running 2.0.35 on my UDB AXP machine.  I'm running the 5.0 version
of ipfwadm.  The rest of my system is 5.1, though.

Help!
Jack.



