Well,
If there is such a beast, then I'm sure it's not from Digital! Digital
Alpha systems are either known as Alphaservers/Alphastations or
DECstations (old Turbochannel-based workstations). The product line
that you call DECservers are actually terminal servers!

What I think you mean is actually called "Digital Server 3300R"..
Is it this one?
http://www.windows.digital.com/products/Server/3300_description.asp

I believe this box is a remarketed Alphaserver 1000A, i.e. from the
NORITAKE family. You didn't say whether it's an EV4 or EV5 model, but
I'll take a guess and say go for the "noritake-s-5" kernel image.

Try it and tell us.

HTH,
Wai-Sun

p.s. DEC and Digital are very different in the product lines... ;-)

