dca2 <jmd@infinet.com> wrote:

> Procedure is:
> copy linload.exe to floppy then rawwrite milo to it.
> rawrite boot and ramdisk to seperate floppys.

Here's where you are having trouble.  milo is an executable, not a disk
image.

You need to:

copy linload.exe to a FAT formated floppy disk, and then copy (not
rawwrite) the milo onto the same floppy.

When you were rawwriting it, you were completely overwriting the
filesystem on the floppy.

-Scott



