: Ok.  This one drove me nuts!

I wonder when I got it when I was doing that for the first time
quite a while ago.  Must be some documentation. :-)

: I have a boot choice called "Boot Linux Floppy".  My load options look like
: this:

: LOADIDENTIFIER=Linux Floppy
: SYSTEMPARTITION=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)
: OSLOADER=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)\linload.exe
: OSLOADPARTITION=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)
: OSLOADFILENAME=\milo
: OSLOADOPTIONS=nodebug
       ^^^^^
    Change this one to 'show' and you will get something useful
instead of an error message.

'linload.exe' loads, by a default, 'milo' from its own directory so
OSLOADFILENAME, SYSTEMPARTITION and OSLOADPARTITION are much less
critical here then they appear in the first place.  What is more,
with ArcBIOS (ARC console on steroids which shows up on some boards
like LX and SX) you cannot set OSLOADFILENAME only a directory to
load it from (default is "\winnt", set it to "\" :-).  You will get
bitching about invalid boot entry which you should totally ignore.


: boot fd0:xl.gz "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1"
                                                    ^^^^^
                           This is harmless but totally superflous.
If you are brave you are putting a string like that into
OSLOADOPTIONS above insted of "nodebug" or "show".  More useful
later for booting automatically from a hard drive.

