One other note here is that you don't want to try to boot the vmlinux file
(although I have never tried).

The file you want when all is said and done with the kernel compile (after
make clean; make dep ; make boot  -as mentioned) is in
/usr/src/linux/arch/alpha/boot

it is "vmlinux.gz"

Personally, I copy this file into my root directory and then point milo to
this file in thebios setup, but you could put it anywhere.

There is no equivalent to needing to run "lilo" on the x86 to make the boot
map, this is handled with milo in the bios or at the milo command prompt.

make sure to "make modules" and "make modules_install" if you chose loadable
module support.

/Mike

