3. Tulip dirver can either be hacked to force the mode you request by going
to the driver (in /usr/src/linux/driver/net/tulip.c) and editing the
"options" array.  It used to be easier, but he has made the driver mutli-card
freindly so now the options are stored in an array called "options" in order
according to the order they are detected and configured by the driver.

see:

