Once you have a running system with loadable modules, then you can edit
/etc/conf.modules to add options to the alias statment for each driver that is
loaded.

The problem you will face is that hacking the driver and passing command line
arguments is a little tough during the install.  If you have the 10BT option,
I would go for it during the install and fix it later from the running
system.

