Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha
Originator: acher@hphalle4.informatik.tu-muenchen.de


Hi,
the DGA-library (libXxf86dga.a) now also works on Alpha. Somebody forgot to add
the _bus_base()-offset of the PCI space to the PCI address before mmap-ing it...
I've looked in the X-server part, to find out how it's properly done: Just
use the glibcAxpIo-library for HW stuff, among other calls it has _bus_base().

The patch and the working library can be found on my homepage:

http://www.informatik.tu-muenchen.de/~acher/linux/

Now even the nagravision decoder (nagratv) works on Alpha :-)

