I had exactly same situation. The solution was to boot to SRM console
and change the time there. Of course I tried the clear all the
settings and got into SRM by accident. Try the command help time or
help date to find out howto do it. To get back to ARC, you must say
set os_type NT 
and boot the computer.  Someone answered already about the 
/etc/sysconfig/clock ARC=true option.

Like this I could save the time to some other year, but anyway I was
able to change it to the correct one in ARC.

Hope this helps.

/Iiro



