even as the complexity has gone and will go further through the roof (EE
times reports 100Million gates in the forseable future (464 I believe was the
basis of thier comment)). 2. Why not, spead freaks are out there and the
software, in the form of linux is catching up quickly.	It needs an office
app on par with MS products.  It needs games, and it needs optimized
compilers, but it has hardware compatability(video card,PCI etc..) and so
long as the market share remains large enough, the cost should be only
slightly more than intel hardware.

