> 2) More importantly, because I can go around the CD using ftp, what could be
> wrong with the partition that minlabel built?

You've encountered a defect introduced in the R.H. 5.1 install. The
install process does not recognize minlabel partitions as being valid.

In a previous posting, another user reported (via a previous posting)
working around this by creating corresponding minlabel and fdisk
partitions on the same disk. I was not able to get this to work. My
solution was to install to a root partition on an fdisk-partitioned
spare drive, then copy to a root partition created using minlabel on my
permanent drive.

Randy C.



