What MB do you have?

What exactl do you mean by "I can boot linux"?	What does it do, how far does
it go?

Assuming you have the correct Milo image for your Alpha MB then the IDE
drivers should be built into Milo.

All you need to do to boot is type the following at the milo prompt (or
program this into your firmware - see "OS setup section of firmare):

boot hdaX:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hdaX

(X, of course is whatever drive holds your kernel and root OS -sdaX for SCSI).

If you have not yet installed linux your boot command line will look more like
this:

boot hda:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hda load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1

of course you need the milo,boot, and root install disks.

Does that answer your question?

/Mike

