 DER> - - - - - - - - -
 DER> Aug  8 15:10:42 linux_box kernel: scsidisk I/O error: dev 08:0c,
 DER> sector 4544
 DER> Aug  8 15:10:44 linux_box kernel: scsi0: MEDIUM ERROR on channel 0,
 DER> id 1, lun 0, CD
 DER> B: Read (10) 00 00 f5 c9 e0 00 00 02 00
 DER> Aug  8 15:10:44 linux_box kernel: Current error sd08:0c: sense key
 DER> Medium Error
 DER> Aug  8 15:10:44 linux_box kernel: Additional sense indicates
 DER> Unrecovered read error

[...]

You have bad blocks on your device /dev/sda12.

It's appened yestersday on my EZ 135

Aug  8 21:08:06 localhost kernel: scsidisk I/O error: dev 08:02, sector 
76106, absolute sector 178710 

Aug  8 21:08:13 localhost kernel: scsi0: MEDIUM ERROR on channel 0, id 1, 
lun 0, CDB: Request Sense 00 00 00 10 00  

Aug  8 21:08:13 localhost kernel: Current error sd08:02: sense key Medium 
Error 

Aug  8 21:08:13 localhost kernel: Additional sense indicates Unrecovered 
read error 

Aug  8 21:08:13 localhost kernel: scsidis 

 DER> /dev/sda12 is the problem drive...
 DER> :)

You need to run e2fsck to check badblocks:

e2fsck -c /dev/sda12

Don't miss to umount the drive.


