I have an Alpha SX164 and Redhat 5.1, too. And I got problems with the
floppies, too. My problem was that linux didn't want to read the RAMDISK
diskette. But you can boot directly from the CD. If you have a CD-ROM
drive, boot MILO from a floppy and enter: boot hdb:kernels/sx164.gz
root=/dev/hdb   (if your CD-ROM drive is hdb). I found this info on the
CD.
I think that the problem is that the kernel detects the floppy as a
2.88M even if it is set to 1.44M in Alphabios. I managed to install
RH5.1, but I can't still read floppies. Hopefully, my local network
works, so I can exchange data.


