>     ipfwadm -F -a m -Smydomain.de/24 -D0/0
> fails with:
>     "setsockopt failed".
> 
> Oh, I used RH5.1 ipfwadm
> 
> Any ideas? Does anyone have a working setup?

You can use the ipfwadm from RedHat-5.0 or the one from ftp.terran.org.
The problem with the RedHat-5.1 one is that glibc includes aren't right.
Some of them (in this case, netinet/ip_fw.h) define packet and byte counts
as u_int32_t, wherease the kernel defines them as "long".  long and
u_int32_t are not the same size on Alpha, so the struct is short, making it
an invalid argument to setsockopt.

cheers,
-bp
--
B. James Phillippe <bryan@terran.org>
Linux Software Engineer, WGT Inc.
http://earth.terran.org/~bryan




