Well, I have looked at these Bytemarks and something seems flakey.
The FPU index seems to be way too low.   Here at the University of
Kentucky physics Dept., a collegue of mine has ported a large Geant
MonteCarlo code from Alpha/DU to Intel/Linux.  This code is heavily
floating point and he did a little comparison between his P2-266 and
my alphastation 200/233.   The alpha ran this code at about 75% the
speed of the P2-266 which seems to be at odds with the Bytemarks.
I'll try to compile the Bytemarks under DU on my alpha for comparison.
Perhaps this is the Alpha/Linux math libraries rearing their ugly heads.

Eric Christy


