>     right to the letters (only at the beginning of a word, though)
>     are still there even at 640x480. This leads me to the assumption that
>     the main problem are the steep signal slopes generated by the ZLXp-E2's
>     BT463 RAMDAC.
> 
> 3.) Use the magnetic damper which comes with the card, right at the SVGA
>     connectors end. No change.
> 
> So I'm currently stuck and put the old 3D10 back in, which is really
> a pitty.
> 
> I think that there *could* be the following ways to solve it:
> 
> a.) Get a better and long video cable and get rid of the extension.
Tom,

If the red shadow is there at all resolutions, it sounds more like the
monitor needs setting up. Convergence error may be the wrong description
if it's a Trinitron, but any monitor that's been out of service for some
time will generally need setting up for pincushion, convergence etc.
Most of the Digital monitors have a trimming tool inside if you take the
lid off.

The advantage of the Trinitron is that they can usually be set up to
almost new quality with a couple of hours works - older, non Trinitron
can be a real no hoper though.

Chris


 
