> your physical pages get spread out in memory you can't cache it all.

I really wish that Linux did page colouring.  For sizes between L1 and
L2, there are often variations like on the starred lines above.
I'm optimising some routines for arithmetic on big polynomials which
get broken down into pieces of this size, typically.  Trying to
optimise in the face of random uncontrollable variations in timing is
difficult to say the least!

Bye,
  Rob.
